+<main id="main-content">
+
+  <section class="policy-hero">
+    <div class="container">
+      <span class="section-eyebrow">Legal</span>
+      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
+      <p>How North Star Technologies collects, uses, stores and protects your personal data.</p>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <section class="policy-body">
+    <div class="container">
+      <div class="policy-content">
+
+        <p class="policy-meta">Effective date: 21 August 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: 21 August 2026</p>
+
+        <div class="policy-note">
+          This Privacy Policy is published in accordance with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act) and the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025, and the Information Technology Act, 2000 read with the Information Technology (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011, as applicable to North Star Technologies as a Data Fiduciary under Indian law.
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="policy-toc">
+          <h2>Contents</h2>
+          <ol>
+            <li><a href="#who-we-are">Who We Are</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#data-we-collect">Personal Data We Collect</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#how-we-use">How and Why We Use Your Data</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#legal-basis">Consent and Legal Basis</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#sharing">Sharing With Third Parties</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#retention">Data Retention</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and Website Analytics</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#security">How We Protect Your Data</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#rights">Your Rights as a Data Principal</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#children">Children's Data</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#grievance">Grievance Redressal</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#board">Complaints to the Data Protection Board of India</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#changes">Changes to This Policy</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#law">Governing Law and Jurisdiction</a></li>
+            <li><a href="#contact-us">Contact Us</a></li>
+          </ol>
+        </div>
+
+        <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who We Are</h2>
+        <p>This website <strong>northstartechnologies.net</strong> is owned and operated by <strong>North Star Technologies</strong> ("North Star", "we", "us", "our"), an ISO 9001:2015 certified technology solutions company with its registered office at 4-157/GF-1, Gayatri Nivas, Kottevari Street, Ramavarappadu, Vijayawada – 521108, Andhra Pradesh, India.</p>
+        <p>For the purposes of the DPDP Act, North Star Technologies is the <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong> in respect of the personal data it collects through this website.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="data-we-collect">2. Personal Data We Collect</h2>
+        <p>We collect personal data only when you choose to share it with us — primarily when you submit an enquiry through our contact form. This includes:</p>
+        <ul>
+          <li>Your full name</li>
+          <li>Company or organization name (optional)</li>
+          <li>Business email address</li>
+          <li>Phone number (optional)</li>
+          <li>The service you are enquiring about</li>
+          <li>The message or project details you provide</li>
+        </ul>
+        <p>We do not knowingly collect financial information, government identity numbers, biometric data, or other sensitive personal data through this website. Please do not include such information in your enquiry message.</p>
+        <p>Our website itself does not use tracking cookies or analytics scripts at this time. If this changes — for example, if we add website analytics — this Policy will be updated in advance and, where required, your consent will be sought.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="how-we-use">3. How and Why We Use Your Data</h2>
+        <p>We use the personal data you provide solely to:</p>
+        <ul>
+          <li>Respond to your enquiry and communicate with you about it</li>
+          <li>Prepare quotations, proposals or consultations you have requested</li>
+          <li>Maintain records of business communications and, where a project proceeds, deliver contracted services</li>
+          <li>Comply with applicable legal, accounting or regulatory obligations</li>
+        </ul>
+        <p>We do not use the information you submit for automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly significant effects concerning you.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="legal-basis">4. Consent and Legal Basis</h2>
+        <p>We process your personal data on the basis of the <strong>consent</strong> you provide when you tick the consent checkbox and submit our contact form. Consent is free, specific, informed and given through a clear affirmative action, in line with Section 6 of the DPDP Act.</p>
+        <p>You may withdraw your consent at any time by writing to us at the contact details in Section 15 below. Withdrawal of consent will not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal, and may affect our ability to respond to a pending enquiry.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="sharing">5. Sharing With Third Parties</h2>
+        <p>We do not sell or rent your personal data. Submissions made through our contact form are transmitted to and stored in a Google Sheet via Google Apps Script, which we use as a data processor to manage enquiries internally. Google processes this data on our behalf under its own security and data-processing terms.</p>
+        <p>We may also share personal data where required by law, in response to a valid legal request from a government or regulatory authority, or with professional advisors (such as accountants or legal counsel) strictly on a need-to-know basis.</p>
+        <p>We do not knowingly transfer personal data outside India except to the extent that our service providers (such as Google) process data on infrastructure located outside India, in which case such transfers are subject to that provider's own compliance safeguards.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="retention">6. Data Retention</h2>
+        <p>We retain enquiry data for as long as necessary to respond to your enquiry, pursue any resulting business relationship, and meet our accounting, tax or legal record-keeping obligations under Indian law — after which it is deleted or anonymized, unless you request earlier deletion under Section 9 below.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies and Website Analytics</h2>
+        <p>This website loads fonts from Google Fonts, which may cause your browser to make a request to Google's servers and share your IP address as part of that request. We do not currently set first-party tracking or advertising cookies, and we do not run analytics scripts. If that changes, we will update this section and, where legally required, present a cookie consent notice.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="security">8. How We Protect Your Data</h2>
+        <p>We follow reasonable security practices and procedures, as required under Section 43A of the Information Technology Act, 2000 and the DPDP Act, including restricting access to enquiry data to authorized personnel, using secure (HTTPS) transmission for this website, and relying on reputable third-party infrastructure (Google) for form storage. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
+        <p>In the event of a personal data breach that is likely to affect you, we will take reasonable steps to notify you and the Data Protection Board of India as required under the DPDP Rules, 2025.</p>
+
+        <h2 id="rights">9. Your Rights as a Data Principal</h2>
+        <p>Under the DPDP Act, 2023, you have the right to:</p>
+        <ul>
+          <li><strong>Access</strong> a summary of the personal data we hold about you and the processing activities we carry out</li>
